                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb11b27d-d043-4c06-b72d-cb6dcd42a3c5",
                                "sense_id": "b332f686-0e07-3fa3-afbe-85931de67d84",
                                "text": "I like to think that the Star, in order to get the benefit of the irony on landlordism, has to digest the irony on dissentism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c29e62cd-6106-4c49-880c-d367450f1c9e",
                                "sense_id": "b332f686-0e07-3fa3-afbe-85931de67d84",
                                "text": "It is the humanities' contribution to the fraternity of mutations in which appear scientism, methodism, democratism, communitarianism, and dissentism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5660ee73-03bf-4a34-9a44-763d90c22416",
                                "sense_id": "b332f686-0e07-3fa3-afbe-85931de67d84",
                                "text": "Rinchan Shah was the ruler of Kashmir at that time, who practiced Buddhism, while his wife, Kota Rani daughter of Ram Chandrina, was a follower of Hindu Dharma. The religious divergences between the two spouses always created the dissentism."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "f94784d2-1707-3488-b070-a40d8233558c",
                "word": "Dissentism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "861c3b54-690f-3fc3-ac8a-158eb1425cd5",
                        "entry_id": "f94784d2-1707-3488-b070-a40d8233558c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The beliefs or practices of the English Dissenters."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9029a2ee-d89f-4843-b30d-908da952e0eb",
                                "sense_id": "861c3b54-690f-3fc3-ac8a-158eb1425cd5",
                                "text": "The natural man will be carried away, and will flit about with the wind of every false doctrine. Protestantism may go over to Puseyism; Dissentism may go over to Congregationalism; and all may merge into Catholicism; but what of all that?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "074e5dcc-e407-43b1-98ce-91d4be6130e4",
                                "sense_id": "861c3b54-690f-3fc3-ac8a-158eb1425cd5",
                                "text": "Is it a second Church-of-England establishment, created out of the taxes, in order to strengthen the patronage of the executive power, according to its imaginary requirements, from the healthy growth of Protestant dissentism?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e8057d4-1d22-40da-88a8-4b8b62057de2",
                                "sense_id": "861c3b54-690f-3fc3-ac8a-158eb1425cd5",
                                "text": "The present study examines an aspect of Green's professional and political life that has been noted but never adequately explained by previous studies — namely, his philo-Dissentism."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
